    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Behavioural idiom</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Null Object</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Replace \"if it is null, skip it\" checks scattered through your code with one small class that implements the interface and does nothing safely: a <code>NullLogger</code>, a <code>NoDiscount</code>, a <code>GuestCustomer</code>. Learn when that is cleaner, when it hides bugs, and how it compares with <code>Optional</code>.</p>\n"
  },
